{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455495-aberrant-new-novas-to-ponder","id":1455495,"title":"[Aberrant] New Novas to ponder","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-24T01:33:59-07:00","id":1455495,"title":"[Aberrant] New Novas to ponder","content":"So the new book has four regional teams of Utopians, said to have 'about ten core members' each, and then lists five to six for each team. Of them, some have been name-dropped a bunch, but never really described in depth, like Griffin Armstrong or Anthony Chang (the only one to go through an arc entirely in *artwork* as he transformed from a short-haired clean cut dude in a T2M unitard to a punker with a red mohawk adorned in spikes chains and leather!) or Allison Pfalzgraff.<br /> <br /> And then there are the new names.<br /> <br /> Force. Nothing else, just a single word! Is Force a dude? A lady? A none-of-your-business, thankyouverymuch? In my headcanon, Force is African-American, because so far the Teams Tomorrow don't have a lot of black faces.<br /> <br /> And Gina Benet. I think I recall that name from somewhere? Wasn't she one of the people who didn't kill Slider? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And Jiro 'Smoke' Kioshi. Does he create smoke and kick your butt when you are stumbling around blind and choking? Is he *made* of smoke? Is it metaphorical and he just 'cannot be captured' like smoke, or, like smoke, leaves behind a blackened haze of destruction after using his fire powers to blow stuff up?<br /> <br /> Argh! It's like the old days of trying to guess whether or not Swarm Queen was a grizzled ex-Elite who turns into acid-dripping flying murder-bugs or a social powerhouse who treated all her Club Zmei patrons as drones in her hive! (Answer, yes, to both!)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","user":"IanWatson","date":". 07-24-2021, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23754-ian-turner","name":"Ian Turner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-24T04:31:41-07:00","id":1455503,"title":"","content":"Simple answer? Do your own meanwhile - and if your homebrew version becomes apocryphal due to evolving canon, make a reveal that (s)he was an impostor all along, letting you introduce the &quot;returned&quot; (canon) version while still having your homebrew one evolve into an active part of your cast/plots!<br /> <br /> Always worked fine for me when messing with canon of 1e Aberrant or WoD games. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> edit: the copycat/impostor does not have to automatically be an antagonist - sometimes an organization might have reasons to want to hide the disappearance of one of its main players, making a replacement for misdirection useful, among other possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-24-2021, 07:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-24T05:31:28-07:00","id":1455505,"title":"","content":"Your character could also have been named in honor of an earlier character with the same name who either died, retired, or disappeared. Happens all the time in comics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-24T07:56:09-07:00","id":1455511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455495-aberrant-new-novas-to-ponder?p=1455505#post1455505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your character could also have been named in honor of an earlier character with the same name who either died, retired, or disappeared. Happens all the time in comics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Easier to happen with heroic nicknames and such, but can definitely possible on the personal, civilian identity level too, as shown by a number of people here and there named after older relatives, living or departed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-24T08:22:04-07:00","id":1455513,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/WkDnN2s.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-24T15:30:02-07:00","id":1455535,"title":"","content":"Oh gosh, the replies make me realize that I fail at communication today. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm not displeased that we have new names being dropped to learn all about as setting information comes out over new releases, I'm excited! I'm all about not just seeing what's changed with our 'old friends' (like Ichiko Iko changing her name to 'Ishin-denshin,' or Cestus Pax who has changed significantly in name, and perhaps backstory and personality) but also get to meet new characters like Force and Smoke.<br /> <br /> I just wanted to speculate despite the total dearth of information on these two. Cause I like to get myself hyped up!<br /> <br /> Smoke seems to be a Japanese dude (and I've already had fun speculating on his 'smoke' powers), but Force is wide open.<br /> <br /> Given that Force is on a team with Cestus Pax, the most intuitive (to me, anyway) idea of making them a flying force-manipulator feels redundant, so perhaps someone who generates glowing golden or blue 'force' constructs that can entrap another (Quantum Attack, entangle), form armor shielding around themself (Quantum Field), or form into barriers and obstructions to hold back mobs or floodwaters or act as a firebreak or temporary structural support (Environmental Anima, barrier). Maybe they can move the force constructs once they create them, and can do the 'ride on a flying force platform' trick to get around. That would make them feel very distinct from just being a second-rate Pax on a team that already has a Pax. Since the team Force is on has two dudes and four ladies, so far, I'd lean towards making him a dude. And with the lowered presence of black men who got some fancy page presence the first time around like Kikjak, Mephistopheleez (another one like Swarm Queen I never really figured out what he did, going from Elite to Novox, so perhaps some powers useful to both career choices?) and Duke 'Core' Baron, I'm also inclined to making him a black man.<br /> <br /> Still, that Proteus Nova Compendium looks fun, thanks for the heads-up Mr. Watson!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23754-ian-turner","name":"Ian Turner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-24T18:00:36-07:00","id":1455547,"title":"","content":"I'd make Force telekinetic, personally (with long range Quantum Anima and Quantum Construct and the like, probably as well as Quantum Field and Quantum Attack, but not a lot of Mega-Attributes)...which differs from your idea mainly cosmetically (and is very different indeed from Pax and what he does), and give Smoke an incorporeal/invisibility/shroud power suite focused on, well, smoke (plus some 'sneaky' Mega-Attribute stuff). Someone other than Figment should be able to play covert operative for Team Tomorrow, IMO.<br /> <br /> For the record, Force, at least, is not actually new, they're mentioned (with no further elaboration...just the one word name/title) in the 1E Project Utopia book. <br /> <br /> My personal assumption for Mephistopheleez was based on him talking about casually beating people up, and was that he was a Mega-Attribute guy, with solid Mega-Physical stuff and a bit of Mega-Social stuff on the side. That'd fit his image, attitude, and career choices pretty well. He never talked about using either weapons or offensive powers, but was an Elite in the classic mercenary sense, so the Mega-Physical stuff seems a solid guess, and the Mega-Social stuff is really just because he became an entertainer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-25T00:34:52-07:00","id":1455558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deadmanwalking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455495-aberrant-new-novas-to-ponder?p=1455547#post1455547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd make Force telekinetic, personally (with long range Quantum Anima and Quantum Construct and the like, probably as well as Quantum Field and Quantum Attack, but not a lot of Mega-Attributes)...which differs from your idea mainly cosmetically (and is very different indeed from Pax and what he does),</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I like that idea, although I *also* would like to make him not too similar to Ragnarockette, who was, at least in the last edition, a telekinetic.<br /> <br /> It amuses me how much I kind of assume about some other members of T2M. Ana Graca Texiera (sp?) can apparently fly and function in outer space (since she's shown in the shuttle rescue mission, flying in space without a suit), and presumably has some superhuman combat abilities (since she fights drug cartels for sport), but I've got no idea if she throws zaps or is more physical (I assume strength, speed and toughness, to go with the flight and life support).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and give Smoke an incorporeal/invisibility/shroud power suite focused on, well, smoke (plus some 'sneaky' Mega-Attribute stuff). Someone other than Figment should be able to play covert operative for Team Tomorrow, IMO. </div> </div> </div>I kind of like the idea that Smoke has more than one of those options, both create smoke and fight while solid but obscured within it (take the Immunity tag so that he can function unimpaired in his own smoke clouds), but also turn into a hot black smoking trail and zip through the air like the demons from Supernatural, being mostly intangible in that state, but able to move fast and fly into people and bowl them over like a strong wind. And Mega-Dex, or even Mega-Stamina, also seem like they'd fit the theme, although I'm wary of making him too much of an on-the-nose ninja trope. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Of course I could steal a 'foxfire' inspired idea and have Smoke able to congeal items out of smoke (like a genie makes stuff out of smokeless fire or a fae spins quasi-real stuff out of 'glamour'), both smaller items like weapons or armor, but also larger items like walls or whatever. (Although that's where I'm leaning for Force, with the energy constructs, and I don't like repeating myself...)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the record, Force, at least, is not actually new, they're mentioned (with no further elaboration...just the one word name/title) in the 1E Project Utopia book. </div> </div> </div>Ooh, cool!<br /> <br /> So many name-drops interest me, like Feathered Serpent, who appeared as a pro-Teragen rally, and later may have destroyed Mexico City, who I want to know more about!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My personal assumption for Mephistopheleez was based on him talking about casually beating people up, and was that he was a Mega-Attribute guy, with solid Mega-Physical stuff and a bit of Mega-Social stuff on the side. That'd fit his image, attitude, and career choices pretty well. He never talked about using either weapons or offensive powers, but was an Elite in the classic mercenary sense, so the Mega-Physical stuff seems a solid guess, and the Mega-Social stuff is really just because he became an entertainer. </div> </div> </div>A sensible set of powers. It amuses me that he might be pretty much a 'stealth nova' with 'just' some Mega-Attributes (despite his larger-than-life attitude, he's more of an Orzaiz than a Duke Baron...), although I'd be inclined to give him Emotion Control as well, inspired by that one picture of him before a crowd, with flames in the background, which makes me think of him as inflaming the crowd as a performer, and using fear, despair or strife-incitement as an Elite.<br /> <br /> This setting has so many fun and inspiring ideas tucked away!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23754-ian-turner","name":"Ian Turner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-25T02:20:47-07:00","id":1455563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ian Turner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455495-aberrant-new-novas-to-ponder?p=1455558#post1455558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I like that idea, although I *also* would like to make him not too similar to Ragnarockette, who was, at least in the last edition, a telekinetic.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Fair. She's also listed as 'invulnerable', though, so some defensive 'always on' stuff (in this edition, probably Mega-Stamina and Toughness, maybe Regeneration as well), on top of telekinesis makes for a pretty big difference. I'd probably give her some other Mega-Attributes as well, while Force would be more of a one trick pony, but probably with more Quantum and better at the trick in question. They're also not on the same team, which makes me less worried about schtick duplication.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ian Turner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455495-aberrant-new-novas-to-ponder?p=1455558#post1455558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It amuses me how much I kind of assume about some other members of T2M. Ana Graca Texiera (sp?) can apparently fly and function in outer space (since she's shown in the shuttle rescue mission, flying in space without a suit), and presumably has some superhuman combat abilities (since she fights drug cartels for sport), but I've got no idea if she throws zaps or is more physical (I assume strength, speed and toughness, to go with the flight and life support).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've personally always pegged her as a Mega-Attribute person as well (flight aside), but I tend to lean that direction for anyone whose powers are not specified despite their deeds being talked about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ian Turner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455495-aberrant-new-novas-to-ponder?p=1455558#post1455558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of like the idea that Smoke has more than one of those options, both create smoke and fight while solid but obscured within it (take the Immunity tag so that he can function unimpaired in his own smoke clouds), but also turn into a hot black smoking trail and zip through the air like the demons from Supernatural, being mostly intangible in that state, but able to move fast and fly into people and bowl them over like a strong wind. And Mega-Dex, or even Mega-Stamina, also seem like they'd fit the theme, although I'm wary of making him too much of an on-the-nose ninja trope. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Of course I could steal a 'foxfire' inspired idea and have Smoke able to congeal items out of smoke (like a genie makes stuff out of smokeless fire or a fae spins quasi-real stuff out of 'glamour'), both smaller items like weapons or armor, but also larger items like walls or whatever. (Although that's where I'm leaning for Force, with the energy constructs, and I don't like repeating myself...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I meant he'd probably have all the options I listed, actually (Phasing + Cloak + Shroud). With Techniques that even works pretty well mechanically in this edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ian Turner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455495-aberrant-new-novas-to-ponder?p=1455558#post1455558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh, cool!</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Yeah, I've been comparing editions and doing some of my own conversions, so I've been on the lookout for this stuff.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ian Turner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455495-aberrant-new-novas-to-ponder?p=1455558#post1455558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So many name-drops interest me, like Feathered Serpent, who appeared as a pro-Teragen rally, and later may have destroyed Mexico City, who I want to know more about!</div> </div> </div> </div>Feathered Serpent is super interesting to me, and I really want to know what he does. He's human looking based on the 1E Teragen book and apparently, at least eventually, quite powerful...and that's all we know. I mean, we know he helped head a rally and that he's a planner as well...so Mega-Social stuff is likely, but that seems very unlikely to be all he has going on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ian Turner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455495-aberrant-new-novas-to-ponder?p=1455558#post1455558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A sensible set of powers. It amuses me that he might be pretty much a 'stealth nova' with 'just' some Mega-Attributes (despite his larger-than-life attitude, he's more of an Orzaiz than a Duke Baron...), although I'd be inclined to give him Emotion Control as well, inspired by that one picture of him before a crowd, with flames in the background, which makes me think of him as inflaming the crowd as a performer, and using fear, despair or strife-incitement as an Elite.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You can do that with Mega-Socials even in 1E. In 2E, there is no more emotion control as its own power, it's all just Mega-Social stuff (specifically, for starting riots, Mega-Presence 2, possibly Compelling Presence, and some level of Mass Influence and maybe Telepresence if you can do it over video), which is more or less what I was thinking he'd have in terms of Mega-Socials, really.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ian Turner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455495-aberrant-new-novas-to-ponder?p=1455558#post1455558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This setting has so many fun and inspiring ideas tucked away!</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely. There's some very cool stuff. Personally, I've been having fun doing conversions of existing 1E characters, particularly those we likely won't see official stats for in this edition, but even including those we probably will. The systems are different enough that it's an interesting exercise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","user":"Deadmanwalking","date":". 07-25-2021, 05:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-26T13:12:54-07:00","id":1455624,"title":"","content":"I'm just getting back into Trinity Continuum after many years away; I'm running a classic Adventure! 1E game but saw how much new material is out and have been picking it up. One Nova I always wanted to build but never did back in the day was Red Bull. He would, of course, have had Morph (to grow wings), Flight (so he can use the wings), and Boost (for obvious reasons). A commercial deal and connections to a Mite ring are, of course, likely....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2173-jvv","name":"JVV","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-26T13:33:43-07:00","id":1455625,"title":"","content":"In 2e, Transformation would be the way to go for that. It covers all three of those. (Well, two, really since Wings give you the ability to fly.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-26T17:19:00-07:00","id":1455631,"title":"","content":"Force has Magnetic Control, but decided on its hero name because &quot;Electro&quot; and &quot;Magneto&quot; were already taken. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-26T21:56:58-07:00","id":1455642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455495-aberrant-new-novas-to-ponder?p=1455631#post1455631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Force has Magnetic Control, but decided on its hero name because &quot;Electro&quot; and &quot;Magneto&quot; were already taken. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Skew (from T2M Americas) already has magnetic powers as his schtick, so this is unsatisfying from a 'balancing out who has what powers' perspective, especially since those are a lot less iconic than more generic telekinesis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T01:49:15-07:00","id":1455646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deadmanwalking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455495-aberrant-new-novas-to-ponder?p=1455642#post1455642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Skew (from T2M Americas) already has magnetic powers as his schtick, so this is unsatisfying from a 'balancing out who has what powers' perspective, especially since those are a lot less iconic than more generic telekinesis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aw, there goes the joke (didn't go far anyway), but yeah, fair points those..... On a more serious note, maybe something related to the absorption and redirection/reflection of kinetic and/or energy attacks perhaps.<br /> <br /> Or maybe i i'm just projecting ideas from my last Teen Tomorrow character, can't say. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T07:27:12-07:00","id":1455655,"title":"","content":"Perhaps this Force guy/lady quantum constructs a Military Force to fight for them? Tanks, manpower, destroyers, you name it!<br /> <br /> They were going to use 'Military Force', but it was too much on the nose and too militaristic, so they shortened it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-29T12:32:59-07:00","id":1455762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455495-aberrant-new-novas-to-ponder?p=1455655#post1455655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps this Force guy/lady quantum constructs a Military Force to fight for them? Tanks, manpower, destroyers, you name it!<br /> <br /> They were going to use 'Military Force', but it was too much on the nose and too militaristic, so they shortened it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>The name is delightfully open to these various interpretations, which is fun.<br /> <br /> 'Force' might be short for 'force multiplier' and they could be a duplicator, or a buffer who renders others in the area temporarily super-effective, or super-coordinated, or mean 'quantum force' and be a kind of 'meta' nova who turns off and on quantum effects and drains quantum points (making them kind of utterly normal when faced with non-Nova threats, but the go-to person for Nova conflicts!).<br /> <br /> Or they could just be mega-Strong and tough, and 'Force' is shorthand for 'brute strength.' The 'Hulk' of the team. It could go a bunch of different ways!<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23754-ian-turner","name":"Ian Turner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-29T22:26:23-07:00","id":1455785,"title":"","content":"Force was one of the people who went into space to go up and fix the shuttle in 1E (and, apparently, needed a space suit to do so), and was noted as helping to 'stabilize the shuttle', so definitely flight and powers useful in that capacity...which is probably not conjuring military forces, though it could easily fit most of the other suggestions that have been made here (including super strength).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-30T02:26:47-07:00","id":1455791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deadmanwalking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455495-aberrant-new-novas-to-ponder?p=1455785#post1455785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Force was one of the people who went into space to go up and fix the shuttle in 1E (and, apparently, needed a space suit to do so), and was noted as helping to 'stabilize the shuttle', so definitely flight and powers useful in that capacity...which is probably not conjuring military forces, though it could easily fit most of the other suggestions that have been made here (including super strength).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Space Force is part of the Military Force, just saying. Also, many of the astronauts are ex-military, so Force could conjure them up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}